/*
 * A deliberately-wrong panel stylesheet. QRPAGER-42.
 *
 * ⚠ THIS FILE EXISTS BECAUSE THE PANEL'S REAL STYLESHEET WAS SCANNED BY NOTHING. Measured
 * before it was written: `apps/api/resources/css/filament/studio/theme.css` -- the file that
 * defines the entire appearance of the studio -- was invisible to `scan-css` (a blanket
 * `apps/api` exemption), to `scan-panel` (its subjects come from the @source globs, which
 * point at the panel PHP and the views, never at the stylesheet) and to `composer guard`
 * (whose scanned paths carry no `resources/`). A raw magenta, an off-ladder padding and an
 * off-scale font size appended to that file were reported CLEAN by all three.
 *
 * Every line below is a form one of the three rules claims to catch. The point is not that
 * the file is wrong; it is that each WAY of being wrong is proven to be caught, so a rule
 * that silently stops matching one syntax fails here rather than in the panel.
 */

/* ---- no-raw-color: every colour syntax CSS offers -------------------------------- */
.hex-six { color: #ff00ff; }
.hex-three { color: #f0f; }
.hex-four { color: #f0fa; }
.hex-eight { color: #ff00ff80; }
.fn-rgb { color: rgb(255, 0, 255); }
.fn-rgba { color: rgba(255, 0, 255, 0.5); }
.fn-hsl { color: hsl(300 100% 50%); }

/*
 * ⚠ `oklch()` IS THE ONE THIS FIXTURE WAS WRITTEN FOR. The grey that `QRPAGER-42` A1
 * replaces is Filament's own `oklch(0.973 0.001 106.424)` on `body.fi-body`, and an
 * override written in the same syntax would have been invisible if `no-raw-color` matched
 * hex alone. It does not -- `color-function` covers it -- and this line is what keeps that
 * true.
 */
.fn-oklch { background-color: oklch(0.973 0.001 106.424); }
.fn-color-mix { color: color-mix(in srgb, #ff00ff, #00ff00); }
.named { color: magenta; }

/* ---- no-raw-spacing: ANY literal, not only an off-scale one ---------------------- */
/*
 * `§12` forbids a hard-coded spacing, not merely an unfashionable one, so BOTH of these are
 * findings: 13 is off the ladder and 16 is on it, and the rule does not care. A version that
 * only caught the off-scale value would let a component type the number for a step instead
 * of naming it, which is the thing the ladder exists to stop.
 */
.spacing-off-ladder { padding: 13px; }
.spacing-on-ladder { padding: 16px; }
.spacing-rem { margin-block-start: 1rem; }
.spacing-gap { gap: 12px; }

/* ---- no-raw-font-size: likewise, any literal ------------------------------------- */
.font-off-scale { font-size: 17px; }
.font-on-scale { font-size: 16px; }
.font-rem { font-size: 1rem; }
